cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "Please cite Version 0.1.0 of this research repository."
title: "Regularly varying mass counts and oscillating spectral asymptotics"
type: software
version: 0.1.0
authors:
  - family-names: Kline
    given-names: Jeffery
license: GPL-3.0-only
abstract: >-
  A paper and release repository on the cylinder operator of a tree of
  intervals, which integrates a function over each interval and adds the
  integral back on that interval. For every child-ratio cap theta in (0,1),
  a bounded-branching tree has interval count D(t) ~ C/t, but the number of
  eigenvalues above t divided by D(t) approaches a continuous nonconstant
  periodic function of log(1/t); the largest possible oscillation over such
  trees is of order theta. Conversely, when D(t) ~ C/t, the eigenvalue count
  is asymptotic to D(t), with no ratio condition beyond a uniform bound below
  one, if the rescaled subtrees are determined by types in a compact space
  whose distribution among the intervals longer than t converges, under a
  continuity condition. The tree of continued-fraction cylinders, whose types
  range over a continuum, satisfies this, with both counts asymptotic to
  6 log 2/(pi^2 t).
keywords:
  - spectral asymptotics
  - compact operators
  - trees
  - regular variation
  - renewal theory
  - continued fractions
references:
  - type: software
    title: "The eigenvalue decay of the limiting kernel of a sparse Mertens matrix"
    version: 0.1.0
    doi: 10.5281/zenodo.23621017
    authors:
